.Dd August 28, 2026
.Dt VMM_NESTED 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vmm_nested
.Nd nested virtualization support in the bhyve hypervisor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "hw.vmm.nested.enable=1"
.Pp
.In machine/vmm.h
.In dev/vmm/vmm_dev.h
.Pp
.Dv VMMCTL_CREATE_NESTED
.Pp
.Dv VMMAPI_OPEN_CREATE_NESTED
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
facility lets
.Xr bhyve 8
expose hardware-assisted virtualization
.Pq Intel VMX or AMD SVM
to a guest, so that a level-1 (L1) guest can act as a hypervisor for
its own level-2 (L2) virtual machines.
.Pp
Two gates must both be open before a guest sees the feature:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.enable
Host-wide switch, default 0.
It can only be set to 1 when
.Va hw.vmm.nested.vmx
or
.Va hw.vmm.nested.svm
reports 2, meaning the host CPU supports what the implementation
needs and the host is not itself a guest;
otherwise the write fails with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
As a
.Xr loader.conf 5
tunable the value is applied after the vendor probe runs.
.It Per-VM opt-in
A virtual machine created through the
.Dv VMMCTL_CREATE_NESTED
ioctl, or through
.Xr vm_create 3
with the
.Dv VMMAPI_OPEN_CREATE_NESTED
flag
.Pq Nm bhyve Fl N ,
carries the
.Va nested_enabled
flag.
VMs created any other way never enter the nested code paths.
.El
.Pp
When both gates are open, CPUID leaf 1 advertises VMX (Intel hosts)
or leaf 0x80000001 advertises SVM and leaf 0x8000000A reports the
emulated SVM feature set (AMD hosts).
.Ss AMD SVM
An L1 hypervisor's
.Dv VMRUN ,
.Dv VMLOAD ,
.Dv VMSAVE ,
.Dv CLGI
and
.Dv STGI
instructions are emulated.
On
.Dv VMRUN
the L1 save area is parked, the L2 save area from the guest VMCB is
loaded into the hardware VMCB together with the union of L0's and
L1's intercepts, and L2 runs until an exit that L1 asked to intercept
(intercept vectors, IOPM or MSRPM).
That exit is then delivered to L1 exactly as hardware would: the L2
state and exit information are written to the guest VMCB, L1 resumes
after
.Dv VMRUN
with GIF clear.
Exits L1 did not ask for are handled by L0 on L2's behalf.
.Pp
When L1 enables nested paging for its guest, L2 runs under a per-vCPU
shadow of L1's nested page table that L0 fills on demand from L2 nested
page faults and discards when L1 requests a TLB flush or switches
.Dv N_CR3 ;
faults L1's table cannot resolve are reflected to L1 as nested page
faults of its guest.
When L1 runs its guest without nested paging, L2 guest-physical
addresses are L1 guest-physical addresses and L0's own table applies.
The SVM feature leaf advertises nested paging and NRIPS only; AVIC, LBR
virtualization, flush-by-ASID and VMCB clean bits are not offered.
.Ss Intel VMX
.Dv VMXON ,
.Dv VMXOFF ,
.Dv VMPTRLD ,
.Dv VMPTRST ,
.Dv VMCLEAR ,
.Dv VMREAD ,
.Dv VMWRITE ,
.Dv VMCALL ,
.Dv INVEPT
and
.Dv INVVPID
are emulated with architectural operand decoding and the
VMsucceed/VMfail conventions of the SDM.
L1's VMCS is kept as a private per-vCPU copy that is written back to
guest memory whenever the current VMCS changes; no L1-supplied value is
ever written into the hardware VMCS.
.Pp
Entering an L2 guest is not implemented yet:
.Dv VMLAUNCH
and
.Dv VMRESUME
pass the instruction-level checks and then complete as a
.Dq VM-entry failure due to invalid guest state
delivered to L1 through the VMCS host-state area, which every L1
hypervisor treats as a fatal error for that L2 guest.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width "hw.vmm.nested.svm_timer_fastpath"
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.enable
Host-wide gate, see above.
Writable at runtime and settable as a
.Xr loader.conf 5
tunable.
The default is 1.
Setting it to 0 disables nesting for virtual machines created afterwards;
machines already running are unaffected.
Writing 1 on a host whose preflight gate failed returns
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
rather than silently doing nothing.
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.vmx , Va hw.vmm.nested.svm
Read-only vendor probe status: 0 unsupported, 1 the host is itself a
guest, 2 ready.
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.vmx_l2
Intel only.
Run L2 guests on hardware.
The default is 1; setting it to 0 falls back to a synthetic
entry-failure path, which is a debugging aid rather than a supported
mode.
Still subject to
.Va hw.vmm.nested.enable .
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.l2stats
Read-only Intel L2 counters: VM entries, events injected into L2,
events swallowed, and events re-delivered after an exit interrupted
their delivery.
A non-zero swallow count indicates lost interrupts.
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.svm_l2inj
Read-only AMD histogram of the interrupt vectors injected into L2,
together with the event-queue counters.
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.svm_debug
Log the first few hundred nested-SVM events per vCPU (VMRUN, exits
reflected to L1, L2 page faults) to the console.
Slow; bring-up only.
The default is 0.
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.svm_timer_fastpath
AMD only.
Answer an L2 guest's i8254 and ACPI timer port reads in
.Nm
rather than reflecting them to the guest hypervisor.
The default is 1.
.It Va hw.vmm.nested.svm_evtq_defer
Test knob.
Carry every requeued L2 event one extra entry through the per-vCPU
event queue, to exercise the queue's ordering.
Not for normal use.
The default is 0.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vm_create 3 ,
.Xr vmm 4 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr bhyve 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
Nested virtualization support first appeared in the CloudBSD
.Fx 16.0-CURRENT
tree.
.Sh BUGS
The feature is experimental and off by default.
L2 execution exists only on AMD; live migration and snapshots of nested
VMs are not supported.
